SUMMARY:What is an OSS Ecosystem Steward\, and can we have one? — Salve J
 . Nilsen
LOCATION:Track A
DESCRIPTION:登壇者: Salve J. Nilsen\nhttps://fortee.jp/yapc-tokyo-2026/p
 roposal/71b322a4-14f5-42d9-bac6-18a9956019c4\n\nThe EU Cyber Resilience Ac
 t (CRA) introduces a new entity dedicated to sustaining and securing Open 
 Source projects: the OSS Steward.\n\nThis organization is meant to support
  projects in many ways – including helping attest their software is inte
 nded for commercial use\, and to be the single contact point towards marke
 t authorities\, CSIRTs\, and manufacturers wishing to remain CRA compliant
 .\n\nIn many ecosystems\, existing foundations may offer this help. But fo
 r Perl and CPAN\, there is no central organization that is both capable an
 d willing to assume the responsibilities of a Steward. So how can we still
  support all who intend to continue make\, rely on\, and benefit from OSS\
 , Perl and CPAN?\n\nHere\, Salve presents his solution – a non-profit co
 mmunity-owned cooperative: the OSS Ecosystem Steward.
URL:https://fortee.jp/yapc-tokyo-2026/proposal/71b322a4-14f5-42d9-bac6-18a9
 956019c4
